---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/cookies/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie Notice for ${siteConfig.siteName} Analytics`}
  description={`How ${siteConfig.siteName} uses cookies: Google’s certified AdSense GDPR CMP in EEA/UK/CH, and the site cookie bar elsewhere. Consent Mode v2.`}
  path={path}
  noindex={true}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Cookies', path }]} />
  <h1>Cookie notice</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Our document generators do not require cookies to fill forms, preview documents, or export PDF/DOCX.
    Everything in the editor runs in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use cookies for</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies and similar storage fall into two buckets on this site: (1) analytics (GA4 when configured), and
    (2) advertising cookies only if Google AdSense is enabled in site configuration. Generators themselves rely
    on in-page JavaScript and optional <code>localStorage</code> drafts—not cookies—to work.
  </p>

  <h2>Which consent tool you see</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>EEA, United Kingdom, and Switzerland:</strong> when AdSense is enabled, we use Google’s
    certified Privacy &amp; messaging GDPR consent message (Funding Choices / adsbygoogle.js, IAB TCF v2.2).
    That is the only consent UI for those visitors. The site’s own Accept/Reject cookie bar is not shown there,
    so you do not get two popups. Analytics and ad storage stay denied until that CMP (or Accept when ads are off)
    updates consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Everywhere else:</strong> the site cookie bar shows Accept and <strong>Reject / Do not sell or
    share</strong>. Analytics is on by default in these regions; Reject / Do not sell or share turns it off and
    remembers your choice.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and Consent Mode</h2>
  <p>
    If Google Analytics (GA4) is configured, Consent Mode v2 sets region-specific defaults before the tag
    configures. For EEA/UK/CH, defaults deny <code>analytics_storage</code>, <code>ad_storage</code>,
    <code>ad_user_data</code>, and <code>ad_personalization</code> until Google’s CMP updates consent. For all
    other countries, those signals default to <strong>granted</strong> so basic traffic measurement works; the GA
    script loads promptly (not deferred until idle). Choosing <strong>Reject / Do not sell or share</strong>
    updates consent to denied for all four signals.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside EEA/UK/CH, choosing <strong>Accept</strong> stores <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=1</code> in
    localStorage and keeps storage granted. Choosing <strong>Reject / Do not sell or share</strong> stores
    <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=0</code> and denies storage (the tag may still load for cookieless pings only).
    Clearing site data shows the bar again. That localStorage key is an internal preference flag, not a
    third-party tracking cookie.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is off unless explicitly enabled in site configuration. When ads are on, Google and partners
    may set advertising cookies as described in the
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. Personalized ads in EEA/UK/CH go through the Google-certified CMP
    message above.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can limit personalized ads via
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>
    and industry opt-outs at
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Local drafts (not cookies)</h2>
  <p>
    Optional “save draft” controls store form field values in <code>localStorage</code> on your device so you can leave a tool
    and return later. Those drafts are not sent to our servers. Clearing site data or using each tool’s clear-draft control
    removes them. Draft keys are separate from the cookie-consent preference described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    In EEA/UK/CH, use Google’s consent message controls. Elsewhere, use the on-site Accept or Reject / Do not
    sell or share controls, then browser settings to block or delete cookies if you change your mind. Rejecting
    analytics does not disable the document generators. For corrections or privacy questions, see
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
